1
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:08,540
A carpenter builds a roof truss.

2
00:00:08,590 --> 00:00:14,560
Two parallel beams are joined by a sloping strut, and one angle is marked 64 degrees.

3
00:00:14,610 --> 00:00:18,360
The truss also contains an isosceles triangle.

4
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:25,280
Which facts will help to find the other angles: parallel-line and triangle facts, or only Pythagoras?

5
00:00:25,330 --> 00:00:28,540
Pause the video and choose.

6
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:31,360
Parallel-line facts and triangle facts.

7
00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:34,580
Pythagoras finds lengths, not angles.

8
00:00:34,630 --> 00:00:41,420
Remember: angles on a straight line add up to 180 degrees, and around a point to 360.

9
00:00:41,470 --> 00:00:44,400
Vertically opposite angles are equal.

10
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:49,860
A triangle's angles add to 180, and a quadrilateral's to 360.

11
00:00:49,910 --> 00:00:54,810
Where a line crosses two parallel lines, corresponding angles are equal.

12
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:56,810
They make an F shape.

13
00:00:56,860 --> 00:01:01,010
Co-interior angles are between the lines, on the same side.

14
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:05,260
They make a C shape, and they add up to 180 degrees.

15
00:01:05,310 --> 00:01:05,990
Your turn.

16
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:08,330
Alternate angles make a Z shape.

17
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:11,920
Are they equal, or do they add up to 180 degrees?

18
00:01:11,970 --> 00:01:14,560
Pause and choose.

19
00:01:14,610 --> 00:01:16,580
Alternate angles are equal.

20
00:01:16,630 --> 00:01:20,570
Only co-interior angles add up to 180 degrees.

21
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:23,020
Real problems need a chain of facts.

22
00:01:23,070 --> 00:01:28,950
Write the reason for each step, like alternate angles, or angles in a triangle.

23
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,290
Here is the method.

24
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:34,520
Step 1: mark all the angles you know on the diagram.

25
00:01:34,570 --> 00:01:40,030
Step 2: look for parallel lines, triangles, straight lines and points.

26
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:44,850
Step 3: find one angle at a time, and give a reason each time.

27
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:49,290
Step 4: check that the angles add up where they should.

28
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:54,090
A transversal makes an angle of 72 degrees with a parallel line.

29
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:58,510
The alternate angle, inside a triangle, is also 72 degrees.

30
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:02,440
The triangle has another angle of 50 degrees.

31
00:02:02,490 --> 00:02:08,000
So the third angle is 180 minus 72 minus 50, which is 58 degrees.

32
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:11,030
Reason: angles in a triangle.

33
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:11,750
Your turn.

34
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:15,490
An isosceles triangle has a top angle of 40 degrees.

35
00:02:15,540 --> 00:02:17,220
What is each base angle?

36
00:02:17,270 --> 00:02:20,210
Pause and work it out.

37
00:02:20,260 --> 00:02:23,120
The two base angles are equal.

38
00:02:23,170 --> 00:02:28,610
180 minus 40 is 140, and half of 140 is 70 degrees.

39
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:34,160
A parallelogram has neighbouring angles of 3 X and 2 X plus 20.

40
00:02:34,210 --> 00:02:37,150
Neighbouring angles add up to 180.

41
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:40,230
So 5 X plus 20 is 180, and X is 32.

42
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:43,690
The angles are 96 and 84 degrees.

43
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:47,430
Two co-interior angles lie between parallel lines.

44
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:48,850
One is 110 degrees.

45
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:50,420
Sara finds the other.

46
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:52,460
Which line is wrong?

47
00:02:52,510 --> 00:02:53,770
Line 1 is wrong.

48
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:57,670
Co-interior angles add up to 180 degrees.

49
00:02:57,720 --> 00:03:01,760
180 minus 110 is 70 degrees.

50
00:03:01,810 --> 00:03:11,310
Carpenters and surveyors use parallel-line angle facts every day, to cut joints that fit, and to lay out roads that cross railways.

51
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:12,670
One last question.

52
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:17,130
Angles on a straight line are 2 Y plus 10, and 3 Y minus 5.

53
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:17,660
Find Y.

54
00:03:17,710 --> 00:03:21,100
Pause the video and answer.

55
00:03:21,150 --> 00:03:23,070
They add up to 180.

56
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:28,370
5 Y plus 5 is 180, so 5 Y is 175, and Y is 35.

57
00:03:28,420 --> 00:03:33,930
To remember: corresponding angles, F, and alternate angles, Z, are equal.

58
00:03:33,980 --> 00:03:38,200
Co-interior angles, C, add up to 180 degrees.

59
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:42,110
Chain the facts, one step at a time, with reasons.

60
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:46,150
The base angles of an isosceles triangle are equal.

61
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:51,430
Great work! Now practise lesson 5.1 on Camday.
